# App Router conventions

Read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before changing routing, metadata, or data APIs — this project uses Next.js 16 with breaking differences.

## Folder layout

```
app/
  layout.tsx, providers.tsx, globals.css
  (site)/     → marketing + catalog routes
  (legal)/    → faq, policies, privacy, terms
  api/        → route handlers only
```

- Route groups `(site)` and `(legal)` organize files only; URLs stay flat (`/about`, not `/(site)/about`).
- New pages go inside `(site)` or `(legal)`, not at `app/` root (except layout, api, sitemap, robots).
- Client providers live in `app/providers.tsx`; context implementations in `context/`.
- Pages are Server Components by default; add `"use client"` only when needed.

## Metadata

- Use `buildMetadata()` from `lib/seo` for page metadata.
- Use `generateStaticParams` for `[slug]` routes backed by `lib/data`.
